#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""archivist-weekly-landed.py -- the weekly "what landed on its own" review.

Owner directive 2026-08-10: autonomy is being widened, so oversight moves from
a per-item approval gate to a weekly retrospective with per-card revert. This
job is that retrospective.

It reads the archivist lane's decisions.log for the last 7 days and buckets
every verdict by who made it:

    auto-gear   -> promoted autonomously (a granted gear acted while Owner slept)
    auto-taste  -> rejected autonomously (an owner-declared auto-reject class)
    anyone else -> the owner's own hand, or a relay carrying his verdicts

plus anything the screen or the taste flagged that QUEUED instead of acting.

It also reports, per card type over the trailing 30 days, how many cards the
gear landed and how many of those were later reverted (a `retired` verdict).

Output is two things:
  1. a Notion page under the hub Archivist parent page, with a table of what
     landed on its own (slug, type, why-this-matters, promotion commit, source)
  2. a compact HTML Telegram message with the counts, the landed card names,
     a URL button to the page, and the revert instruction

Contract:
  - Python 3 stdlib only (hub ships 3.9). No model calls. Deterministic.
  - Read-only against the vault: it never writes knowledge/ or the lane.
  - Exits nonzero ONLY on real failure (unreadable log, Notion refused), so
    cron-run-hub.sh alerts. An empty week is a normal short message, exit 0.
  - No em dashes anywhere in the Notion page or the Telegram message: any
    that arrive inside quoted card text are normalized on the way through.

Usage:
    archivist-weekly-landed.py [--days N] [--dry-run] [--no-telegram]

    --dry-run     build everything, print it, publish nothing, send nothing
    --no-telegram publish the Notion page but skip the Telegram send

Scheduled Sundays 17:00 PT by launchd job com.sov.cron.archivist-weekly-landed
via cron-run-hub.sh (no --deliver: this script sends its own message).
"""

